{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אלה בני אפרים", :translit "eleh bnei efrayim", :gloss "these are the sons of Ephraim"} {:he "בבני אפרים כתיב אלה", :translit "bivnei efrayim katuv eleh", :gloss "in 'the sons of Ephraim' it is written eleh"} {:he "אלה אלהיך ישראל", :translit "eleh elohekha yisra'el", :gloss "your god, O Israel"} {:he "אלה בבני דן", :translit "eleh bivnei dan", :gloss "these in the sons of Dan"} {:he "ויתן את האחד בדן", :translit "vayiten et ha-echad be-dan", :gloss "and he set the one in Dan"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the word אלה in the tribal register echoes אלה in Jeroboam's declaration about the golden calves"}], :frame {:text "Jeroboam son of Nebat led the northern tribes into sin by making two golden calves, declaring to Israel 'Behold your god, O Israel, who brought you up from the land of Egypt' (1 Kings 12:28). He placed one in Bethel and the other in Dan (1 Kings 12:29). Jeroboam descended from the tribe of Ephraim, son of Joseph (1 Kings 11:26). The Ba'al HaTurim links the word אלה in the census of Ephraim to the identical word אלה in Jeroboam's declaration, and notes a parallel usage of אלה in the census of Dan, the site of one of the calves.", :sources ["1 Kings 12:28" "1 Kings 12:29" "1 Kings 11:26"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the word אלה in the tribal register echoes אלה in Jeroboam's declaration about the golden calves", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:31:43.812340823Z", :model "glm-5.2"}